  "description": {
   "extraction_status": "extracted",
   "value": "The study investigated neural correlates of preparatory control when participants anticipated using expressive suppression or cognitive reappraisal to regulate upcoming negative emotions, and examined how preparatory activity related to regulation during the subsequent emotional image.",
   "value_source": "generated"
  },
  "design": {
   "extraction_status": "extracted",
   "value": "Event-related functional magnetic resonance imaging was recorded in 42 female participants while they completed a three-condition emotion-regulation paradigm. Participants were cued to suppress, reappraise, or appraise negative high-arousing images during separate cue and target phases.",
